From 6fd9d7b5b5f7c33f8fd75f1ec36f5339c59e7b5e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: fabian <fabian.maass@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 30 Dec 2025 21:31:55 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] feat(blacklist): add 2-way blocklist sync with automatic
 enforcement
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

- Implement bidirectional sync between Seerr blacklist and Radarr/Sonarr exclusions
- Add automatic enforcement: detect and remove blocklisted media from arr services
- Create discovery API endpoint and script to find existing violations
- Add enforcement toggle in Radarr/Sonarr settings UI with per-server control
- Schedule hourly sync job (configurable interval via settings)
- Add API methods to programmatically manage Radarr/Sonarr exclusions
- Prevent blocklisted media from being requested (throws BlacklistedMediaError)
- Add enhanced logging for API key authentication and permission checks
- Integrate with existing watchlist sync for blocklist awareness

Technical implementation:
- Core sync engine in server/lib/blocklistSync.ts (~991 lines)
- Radarr/Sonarr specific handlers with exclusion management APIs
- Settings integration with blocklistSyncEnabled and blocklistSyncInterval
- Job scheduler registers blocklist-sync job with hourly default
- Discovery script (pnpm blacklist:discover) for read-only violation detection
- Settings UI adds enforcement checkboxes per Radarr/Sonarr server
- MediaRequest.request() checks Seerr blacklist before allowing requests

Test:
- Settings → Radarr/Sonarr → Enable 'Enforce Blocklist' checkbox
- API: POST /api/v1/settings/blocklist/violations
- Script: pnpm blacklist:discover
